NAME
    date - print the current date and time

SYNOPSIS
    date
    date --advjson

DESCRIPTION
    Reads the Unix epoch via SYS_TIME (the NTP-corrected wall clock —
    see session 60) and prints a human-readable form:

      Sat May 17 11:25:30 UTC 2026

    The OS keeps time in UTC. Time zones aren't modeled.

    --advjson emits one JSONL record with: unix (epoch seconds),
    iso (ISO-8601 string), year, month, day, hour, minute, second.

EXAMPLES
    date
    date |> pluck unix                  # epoch as a single line

EXIT STATUS
    0   always

SEE ALSO
    pluck(1)

NOTES
    The RTC is read at boot and NTP-synced periodically (kernel
    /proc/ntp shows sync status). Without a working NTP server in
    the QEMU NAT environment, the OS uses whatever the BIOS RTC
    says when the VM started.
